One note on a detail I could not fully pin down: [38;5;10mregister int y[0m and the signed-overflow cases are technically UB in C, so "byte-identical" there means identical to what [38;5;10mgcc -O2[0m produced on this machine, not something guaranteed by the standard. If the reference binary is built with a different compiler or optimization level, the overflow cases are the ones worth re-checking; the well-defined inputs are unaffected.[0m[0m
